{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T21:06:25.972Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b343c237d9dd86b74913bb91","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1rfy0y","claim:pm-btv6x7","claim:pm-gh1631","claim:pm-wftvem","claim:pm-y4v90c","lineage:pm-gh1631","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-1rfy0y+pm-btv6x7+pm-gh1631+pm-wftvem+pm-y4v90c","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1rfy0y","claim:pm-btv6x7","claim:pm-gh1631","claim:pm-wftvem","claim:pm-y4v90c","lineage:pm-gh1631","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-01T21:06:25.972Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation (src/sdk/test/update.ts): a command or cmd key in --set-json or in the SDK patch is refused with linked_test_command_immutable and changed:false, under the item lock and before any write. When the patch names a new non-empty command, recovery.suggested_retry_args is one scope-preserving invocation: pm --pm-path <tracker> test <id> --remove command=<exact current command> --add-json <entry>. The removal falls back to --remove-index <locked position> when the entry has no unique command. The entry keeps the selected test's editable metadata, overlaid with the patch's other fields, and gets the new command. That is the existing atomic remove+add path: one tests_add history event, fresh provenance, other entries untouched, replacement appended at the end. Repeating the current command or sending an empty one gets the same code with a pointer to the editable fields instead. Other unsupported keys (provenance, editor stamps, unknown keys, the timeout alias) now refuse with linked_test_patch_fields_unsupported, with recovery.allowed_values listing the editable fields and field naming the first offender. The message text is unchanged.\n\nProof (tests/integration/linked-tests/linked-test-editing.integration.spec.ts): the SDK and CLI refusals leave bytes unchanged. Executing the CLI's advertised retry replaces only the selected entry (the untouched entry deep-equals its prior state), adds exactly one tests_add event, and history --verify --strict-exit passes. The same-command, empty-command, unsupported-field, empty-patch and legacy path-only (index fallback) cases are covered too. MCP and PmClient share the same SDK function.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T21:06:25.972Z"}],"before_hash":"7147d71747f242c3edee6a4dbb4971433ad7e5149195299980583ec5bdd35dab","after_hash":"54670666813a7368de59bdf80e5a1c61cd79d45c7ba78a7915ab0985f3ab74a2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"31b8287e173b78252735258c348675e0606f3267bc12122e3d0d3108c34993ae"}
